+Renders voxel worlds by storing per-voxel attributes (position, material, orientation) in a GPU-accessible Shader Storage Buffer Object (SSBO) or Structured Buffer, and rendering them via a single instanced draw call using a shared base geometry primitive. It solves the performance bottleneck of generating and uploading individual mesh geometry for millions of voxels by moving attribute resolution and transformation into the vertex shader. It is distinguished from [Surface-based Instancing with Noise Modulation](1582-surface-based-instancing-with-noise-modulation.md) by its explicit geometric rasterization of voxels rather than procedural surface approximation, and from [3D Gaussian Splatting via Instancing](1586-3d-gaussian-splatting-via-instancing.md) by its use of hard-edged cubic primitives rather than soft volumetric splats.
 
 ### Indirect Draw Argument Setting
-- **Definition**: A compute shader kernel that sets up indirect draw arguments by multiplying vertex and instance counts and setting start indices [S1, unofficial].
